#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:266
msgid "How to import demo content"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:271
msgid "First install the \"One Click Demo Import\" plugin on the website"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:272
msgid "One Click Demo Import plugin page"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:280
msgid ""
"Once you have installed and activated the plugin, go to your WordPress "
"Dashboard under \"Appearance-> Import Demo Data\" and click on the \"Import "
"Demo Data\" button. Please click on the Import button only once and wait, it "
"can take a couple of minutes."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:281
#: inc/demo-import/demo-import-settings.php:11
msgid ""
"We recommend importing the demo content to new websites without content. "
"This is to avoid filling the website with new pages and posts that could "
"create confusion with existing content. After you import the demo, the main "
"menu, widgets, and some parts of the theme (like the site logo) must be set "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:293
msgid "How to set the \"one page\" template in the home page"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:298
msgid ""
"Watch the video to set the onepage template on the home page, or read the "
"step-by-step instructions below."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:301
#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:367
msgid "Link to the YouTube video"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:306
msgid ""
"1) Create a new page and name it as you like (eg. My Home Page). In the "
"\"Page Attributes\" section choose the template called \"One Page Website\" "
"and save the page."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:314
msgid ""
"2) Go in your WordPress Dashboard under \"Settings-> Reading\". Set the "
"\"Front page displays\" on \"Static Page\" and choose the page you "
"previously created as Front page (eg. My Home Page)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:322
msgid ""
"3) Perfect! Now you can go in your WordPress Dashboard under \"Appearance-> "
"Customize\" and you'll see the section called \"Elementare Onepage\" in "
"which you can customize the home page."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:334
msgid "One Page: how to scroll to section using the menu"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:339
msgid ""
"1) Go to your WordPress Dashboard under \"Appearance-> Customize-> "
"Elementare Onepage\" and choose one section (eg. Features) and add a section "
"ID (eg. features) for this section. Save the options."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:347
msgid ""
"2) Now go to your WordPress Dashboard under \"Appearance-> Menus\" and "
"create a new custom link with the URL of your home page followed the ID "
"created for the section (eg. yoursite.com/#features). Add this custom link "
"to your menu and save the options."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:359
msgid ""
"One Page: how to set \"About Us\" section, \"Features\" section, \"Services"
"\" section and \"Team\" section"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:364
msgid ""
"Watch the video to set the \"About Us\" section, or read the step-by-step "
"instructions below."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:372
msgid ""
"1) These sections (About Us, Features, Services and Team) work in the same "
"way and with the same procedure. To insert the content create a new page, "
"and insert the title, content and featured image. The featured image is only "
"valid for the \"About Us\" and \"Team\" section but is not mandatory."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:380
msgid ""
"2) Now go to \"Appearance-> Customize-> Elementare Onepage\" and choose the "
"section you want to edit (About Us, Features or Services). Find the option "
"called \"Choose the page to display\" and search the page you just created."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:388
msgid ""
"3) Now the section will show the content of the page previously created and "
"the layout will be like the example image. The \"Features\", \"Services\" "
"and \"Team\" sections work in the same way but will have a different layout."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:400
msgid "One Page: how to re-order sections"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:405
msgid ""
"Re-order sections is available in Elementare PRO version. With this feature "
"you can choose the position of each section using drag and drop. Click on "
"the button below for more information:"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:406
msgid "More Info About PRO Version"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:418
msgid "How to add social icons"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:423
msgid ""
"Go to your WordPress Dashboard under \"Appearance-> Customize-> Elementare "
"Theme Options-> Social Network\". Here you can choose which social network "
"to show, social icons will be displayed in the footer."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:435
msgid "How to add custom logo"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:440
msgid ""
"Go to your WordPress Dashboard under \"Appearance-> Customize-> Site Identity"
"\". Here you can upload your custom logo (size 250x60px)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:452
msgid "How to change theme colors"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:457
msgid ""
"Go to your WordPress Dashboard under \"Appearance-> Customize-> Elementare "
"Theme Options-> Theme Colors\". Here you can change the theme colors "
"according to sections of the site (header, content, push sidebar and footer)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:469
msgid "How to display page loader"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:474
msgid ""
"Go to your WordPress Dashboard under \"Appearance-> Customize-> Elementare "
"Theme Options-> General Settings\", find the option called \"Display page "
"loader\" and check it. The background will be the same of \"Content "
"background color\" and the loader icon the same color of \"Link color\"."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:486
msgid "Can I use a page builder plugin?"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:491
msgid ""
"Yes, the theme is compatible with Elementor Page Builder, SiteOrigin and "
"Beaver Builder plugins. Just create or edit the page you want to use the "
"page builder and choose the template called \"Full Width for page builders"
"\". This template allows page builders to have maximum page customization "
"(only the menu and the footer will be visible)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:493
msgid ""
"Moreover, in the PRO version, it is possible to use the custom sections to "
"\"import\" entire pages created with the Page Builders inside the Onepage."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:505
msgid "How to highlight a menu item"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:510
msgid ""
"If you need to emphasize a menu item (call to action, donate button, etc..) "
"just go to your WordPress Dashboard under \"Appearance-> Menus\". Create a "
"new \"Custom Links\" and drag it into the menu. Expand the entry and in the "
"\"CSS Classes\" section write: crestaMenuButton"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/elementare-admin-page.php:518
msgid ""
"This will be the result (the colors change according to the ones chosen)."
msgstr ""

